e US government to  using these types of contractors what  about law within the countries that the  contractors operate I mean what what law  applies in those countries since they  don't count as boots on the ground I'm  guessing that  they are not operating within what you  would consider a theater of war or maybe  I'm wrong I don't know well we don't  know the answer so in you know there's  most of these company mercenaries armed  contractors go to conflict markets where  rule of law is already very weak these  are civil wars essentially so for  example in 2007 ten years ago a bunch of  Blackwater mercenaries contractors  killed 17 innocent Iraqis in a traffic  circle in Baghdad called nice or swear  this became one of the low points of the  Iraq war this problem it may have been  the the worst war crime you know done in  the Iraq war by US forces and I'm  including them as US forces there was a  US contract you know what what happened  to them after they murdered civilians  well they got an airplane they went home  that's all that happened to them they  were tried in Iraq they weren't really  they weren't tried in America until  years later and a very controversial  trial and this is the problems of future  if if we had a mercenary working under  the US government in Iraq from a place  like I'll just pick on Guatemala and  that soldiers counterinsurgency  techniques are different than ours and  he massacres and you know a whole family  in Afghanistan where's he go on trial is  it in America is it in Afghanistan is it  you know from his home country or is it  nowhere we still don't know so this is  the problem is that there are is no real  rule of law international laws really  don't apply very well and at the end of  the day who's going to arrest  mercenaries Mercer Hayes will just shoot  the law enforcement when it comes to  some of the other stereotypes that exist  about these types of contractors can you  address number one how the mortality  rate compares for